From d90d9d0216a2f04f263bb239fb3964cbc2340b80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MacScope contributors <contributors@macscope.invalid>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 09:04:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(gst): add host-fed external termio backend

Implement the .external termio backend and wire it end to end:

- backend.zig: extend Kind, Config, Backend, and ThreadData
  exhaustively with .external dispatch; .exec arms are untouched.
- External.zig: the backend implementation. threadEnter registers the
  shared wakeup on the existing termio io thread; only that thread
  drains the bounded inbound mailbox into Termio.processOutput, in
  accepted-feed order. queueWrite delivers terminal-generated bytes to
  the host write callback byte-identically (including the exec
  backend's exact linefeed-mode CRLF translation) with a bounded
  pending buffer for host backpressure, edge-latched health events,
  and observable permanent failure on overflow or host close. resize
  proposes exact grid/pixel geometry (validated, duplicate-coalesced)
  and never touches a pty. Host-reported terminal process states close
  the feed channel, preserve the final screen, and deliver exactly one
  close callback from the io thread. getProcessInfo reports neutral
  (null) data: process metadata is host-owned and never fabricated.
- Surface.zig: select the external backend at construction when the
  apprt surface provides externalIoConfig (comptime-eliminated
  elsewhere); external surfaces never construct Exec, an env map, or a
  command. The abnormal-exit command join stays exhaustive.
- apprt/embedded.zig: initExternal construction seam, session-scoped
  close request routing, and the C API: ghostty_surface_new_external
  (fail-closed validation, registry publication),
  ghostty_surface_external_feed,
  ghostty_surface_external_set_process_state, and
  ghostty_surface_is_external_io; ghostty_surface_free unregisters and
  drains in-flight host calls before teardown begins.
- apprt/none.zig: add a no-op App.wakeup so core mailbox paths are
  semantically analyzable under the none runtime used by zig build
  test; required for the new termio integration tests, no behavior
  change.

Integration tests drive the real Termio state headlessly (the harness
plays the io thread deterministically, no sleeps): construction without
exec, hello feeding, chunk-boundary equivalence including split UTF-8
and CSI, inbound backpressure atomicity/recovery with feed_ready,
byte-exact write/reply/focus/linefeed delivery, exact resize proposals,
host exit/signal screen preservation with single close delivery, output
suppression after closure, write-backpressure retry without loss or
duplication, pending overflow failure, and leak-checked
create/feed/close/destroy cycles.

